-- DICT-SEMANTICS §4.1 G4 (#2095): the shipped OVER-REJECTION `docs/KNOWN-GAPS.md`
-- names under "Known over-reject: a plain ground-type local also gets pinned"
-- -- the exact repro quoted there. `s` forwards to the prelude's `debug` and is
-- used at two plain GROUND types with no enclosing polymorphic signature at
-- all: nothing here needs an abstract dictionary, and `s` already looks fully
-- monomorphic per use. It is rejected anyway, by the same
-- `T-LOCAL-CONSTRAINED-MONO` pin as the two rows above, because the pin cannot
-- tell "needs abstraction" apart from "is merely reused". Fix order #2032,
-- blocked on #1046 per KNOWN-GAPS.md. Pinned KNOWN-BAD, not to the spec's
-- accept.
main =
  let s = v => debug v
  println (s 1)
  println (s True)
